<title>SOUTH KOREA: Record number of stocks end lower on Seoul bourse.</title>
<headline>Record number of stocks end lower on Seoul bourse.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>An all-time record 920 stocks fell during Thursday's trading, the Korea Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>Only 64 stocks advanced.</p>
<p>The bourse ended the day's trading down 18.75 points to a provisional 659.01.</p>
<p>Brokers said investment sentiment was hammered by union unrest, unleashed by the passage of a new labour law.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
